{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0b8736027d5d31874c6dfd5bbfc7c6ef3ad538b94d632943ad10beb984404265"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README requires Python 3.9 or later but below 3.12, and instructs installing node and pnpm before actual use; installation is possible via pip, an editable git clone, or Docker."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0e7551934ea117c3f98cd03e416d2af2727ac1efb137fa221ab5c642eabc6cf3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A DataInterpreter role (metagpt.roles.di.data_interpreter) can be run asynchronously with a natural-language task such as analyzing the sklearn Iris dataset with a plot."},{"claim_ids":["clm_963905395c9f1dde28c904350d4c6a38f68edea0b737bba4ddb5301db8e2c355"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product exposes a CLI: running `metagpt \"Create a 2048 game\"` generates a repository in ./workspace."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a064ad78d4e9c3be24b97956392ef696a38d8730b5120f2c65f0a97519f8795e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration is initialized with `metagpt --init-config`, creating ~/.metagpt/config2.yaml which users edit; the example config supports api_type values like openai, azure, ollama, and groq with model, base_url, and api_key fields."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ab15aab1a20e5dcd259cc6632555f753b00a4986a5bfbb32e8518c12b3b71e87"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MetaGPT takes a one-line requirement as input and outputs artifacts such as user stories, competitive analysis, requirements, data structures, APIs, and documents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cd843948ea7ceb4160ab60df2728d0dd571866c25d1973d08b0811a7719b102c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MetaGPT can also be used as a Python library via `metagpt.software_company.generate_repo`, which returns a ProjectRepo whose structure can be printed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cf7a281f5f1048638a9e09ddbfdeb3c9e6af2d3bb23a8ca96f1db8ef5432c36c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is MIT-licensed, open-sourced June 2023, and its ICLR 2024 paper on multi-agent collaborative meta programming is cited alongside related work such as AFlow, SPO, AOT, FACT, and SELA."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ee0bf87e7958b9e6e6c4768e142b2f5813035055eb90a93bdff5f15f4500486d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Internally the system models a software company with product manager, architect, project manager, and engineer roles orchestrated via SOPs, summarized by the philosophy 'Code = SOP(Team)'."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0b8736027d5d31874c6dfd5bbfc7c6ef3ad538b94d632943ad10beb984404265","clm_0e7551934ea117c3f98cd03e416d2af2727ac1efb137fa221ab5c642eabc6cf3","clm_963905395c9f1dde28c904350d4c6a38f68edea0b737bba4ddb5301db8e2c355","clm_a064ad78d4e9c3be24b97956392ef696a38d8730b5120f2c65f0a97519f8795e","clm_ab15aab1a20e5dcd259cc6632555f753b00a4986a5bfbb32e8518c12b3b71e87","clm_cd843948ea7ceb4160ab60df2728d0dd571866c25d1973d08b0811a7719b102c","clm_cf7a281f5f1048638a9e09ddbfdeb3c9e6af2d3bb23a8ca96f1db8ef5432c36c","clm_ee0bf87e7958b9e6e6c4768e142b2f5813035055eb90a93bdff5f15f4500486d"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972","id":"pg_25aeb63fdd4e52ed82854d0db27ffe67","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/foundationagents-metagpt-readme-md-11cdf466d042-4d0db27ffe67.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_de73073561d453b4aaa21d8d677387a3"],"title":"FoundationAgents/MetaGPT/README.md @ 11cdf466d042","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972"}
